# Only used on development. Add your backend URL to which you want to proxy your requests. Check proxy config in vite.config.js for more information

VITE_DEV_BACKEND_URL="http://127.0.0.1:8000"

# Rollbar browser error reporting is configured in src/config/rollbar.ts, not here:
# tokens are resolved at runtime by hostname (src/config/detect-env.ts) because one
# static bundle is served per environment. To turn it on:
#   1. Paste per-env post_client_item tokens into `envTokens` in src/config/rollbar.ts
#      (public, safe to embed -- same as an auth0 clientId).
#   2. Set ROLLBAR_SOURCEMAP_TOKENS (Rollbar post_server_item tokens -- secret, NOT
#      the public ones above) in the build environment so `npm run upload-sourcemaps`
#      can ship the maps to Rollbar, or stack traces stay minified. The build emits
#      hidden source maps, uploads them, then deletes them -- they are never served
#      publicly. AWS: a ROLLBAR_SOURCEMAP_TOKENS GitHub Actions secret (see
#      .github/workflows/app-deploy.yml). Heroku: a ROLLBAR_SOURCEMAP_TOKENS config
#      var (SOURCE_VERSION is set automatically at build time).
#
#      The value is a COMMA-SEPARATED LIST with one post_server_item token per
#      Rollbar project the build can report to. On Heroku the slug is built once (at
#      staging) and promoted unchanged to production, yet reports to a different
#      project per environment (staging vs production are separate projects, resolved
#      at runtime by hostname). Source maps are stored per project, so the one build
#      must seed every project's store. AWS rebuilds a fresh image per environment,
#      so there only that environment's token is strictly needed, but the same list
#      works and simply seeds the others too.
#      Example: ROLLBAR_SOURCEMAP_TOKENS="<staging_post_server_item>,<prod_post_server_item>"
